{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal-record screening limits","requirement":"Before making a conditional offer a housing provider must not ask about or consider an applicant's criminal record; after one it may weigh only listed convictions, give written reasons and an appeal, and may not require drug or alcohol tests.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider, except dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"The pre-offer inquiry ban does not apply to convictions for methamphetamine manufacture or production on federally assisted housing premises or to lifetime sex-offender registration.","coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"Civil penalties up to $1,000; $5,000 for one prior violation in five years; $10,000 for two or more in seven years; up to $1,000 paid to the applicant.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not make any oral or written inquiry regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to making a conditional offer.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application-fee disclosure","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee a housing provider must disclose in writing whether it reviews criminal history and that applicants may submit evidence of inaccuracies or rehabilitation; the director may order the fee returned.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider, except dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"The director may require that the applicant's rental application fee be returned.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1) Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history; and (2) A statement that the applicant, pursuant to subsection a. of this section, may provide evidence demonstrating inaccuracies within the applicant's criminal record or evidence of rehabilitation or other mitigating factors.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act eviction after successful provider appeal","requirement":"If a housing provider's appeal succeeds and a court overturns the director's order, that determination is grounds to evict the former applicant who moved in under the order, on at least 45 days' notice.","key_value":"45 days' notice","coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider, except dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"Applies when the provider's appeal of a director's order succeeds and the former applicant resides in the provider's unit because of that order.","coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction;","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","n_rules":3,"note":null}

